{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F68kvNZjfwgHDpFSfusVVR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/* SPDX-License-Identifier: RedHat */\n2\t/* Copyright (C) 2002,2007 by  Red Hat, Incorporated. All rights reserved. */\n3\t\n4\t/**\n5\t *\n6\t * This macro is used to classify :math:`x`. It can be called with ``float``,\n7\t * ``double`` or ``long double`` input. This macro is implemented in\n8\t * ``math.h``.\n9\t *\n10\t * Synopsis\n11\t * ========\n12\t *\n13\t * .. code-block:: c\n14\t *\n15\t *     #include <math.h>\n16\t *     int fpclassify(x);\n17\t *\n18\t * Description\n19\t * ===========\n20\t *\n21\t * ``fpclassify`` returns different constants depending on whether the input is\n22\t * subnormal, normal, zero, infinite or :math:`NaN`.\n23\t *\n24\t * Mathematical Function\n25\t * =====================\n26\t *\n27\t * .. math::\n28\t *\n29\t *    fpclassify(x) = \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} FP\\_ZERO, & x = \\pm 0.0 \\\\\n30\t *                                             FP\\_SUBNORMAL, & x \\in \\mathbb{S} \\\\\n31\t *                                             FP\\_INFINITE, & x = \\pm Inf \\\\\n32\t *                                             FP\\_NAN, & x = NaN \\\\\n33\t *                                             FP\\_NORMAL, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.\n34\t *\n35\t * Returns\n36\t * =======\n37\t *\n38\t * ``fpclassify`` returns constant values, see ``math.h`` for their specific values.\n39\t *\n40\t * Exceptions\n41\t * ==========\n42\t *\n43\t * Does not raise exceptions.\n44\t *\n45\t * Output map\n46\t * ==========\n47\t *\n48\t * +---------------------+-----------------+------------------------------+------------------------------+-------------+------------------------------+------------------------------+-----------------+-------------+\n49\t * | **x**               | :math:`-Inf`    | :math:`<0 \\notin \\mathbb{S}` | :math:`<0 \\in \\mathbb{S}`    | :math:`±0`  | :math:`>0 \\in \\mathbb{S}`    | :math:`>0 \\notin \\mathbb{S}` | :math:`+Inf`    | :math:`NaN` |\n50\t * +=====================+=================+==============================+==============================+=============+==============================+==============================+=================+=============+\n51\t * | **fpclassify(x)**   | ``FP_INFINITE`` | ``FP_NORMAL``                | ``FP_SUBNORMAL``             | ``FP_ZERO`` | ``FP_SUBNORMAL``             | ``FP_NORMAL``                | ``FP_INFINITE`` | ``FP_NAN``  |\n52\t * +---------------------+-----------------+------------------------------+------------------------------+-------------+------------------------------+------------------------------+-----------------+-------------+\n53\t *\n54\t */\n55\t\n56\t#include <math.h>\n57\t#include \"../../common/tools.h\"\n58\t\n59\tint __fpclassifyd(double x)\n60\t{\n61\t    uint32_t msw, lsw;\n62\t\n63\t    EXTRACT_WORDS(msw, lsw, x);\n64\t    msw &= 0x7fffffffU;\n65\t\n66\t    if (msw == 0x00000000U && lsw == 0x00000000U) {\n67\t        return FP_ZERO;\n68\t    } else if (msw >= 0x00100000U && msw <= 0x7fefffffU) {\n69\t        return FP_NORMAL;\n70\t    } else if (msw <= 0x000fffffU) {    /* zero is already handled above */\n71\t        return FP_SUBNORMAL;\n72\t    } else if (msw == 0x7ff00000U && lsw == 0x00000000U) {\n73\t        return FP_INFINITE;\n74\t    } else {\n75\t        return FP_NAN;\n76\t    }\n77\t}\n78\t\n[result-id: r8]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011mmtMYWuYsYyyfdxje3npW","session_id":"d923b022-feac-4b63-bc89-51a1cb4c0215","uuid":"da2cf20c-31b9-444a-98c9-59baeb4829f8","timestamp":"2026-04-07T18:19:56.608Z"}
