\\pi}}\\int_{0}^{x}e^{-t^2}dt` | :math:`+Inf` | :math:`qNaN` |\n50\t * +------------+--------------+-----------------------------------------------------+------------+------------+----------------------------------------------------+--------------+--------------+\n51\t *\n52\t */\n53\t\n54\t/* double erf(double x)\n55\t * double erfc(double x)\n56\t *                 x\n57\t *              2      |\\\n58\t *     erf(x)  =  ---------  | exp(-t*t)dt\n59\t *            sqrt(pi) \\|\n60\t *                 0\n61\t *\n62\t *     erfc(x) =  1-erf(x)\n63\t *  Note that\n64\t *        erf(-x) = -erf(x)\n65\t *        erfc(-x) = 2 - erfc(x)\n66\t *\n67\t * Method:\n68\t *    1. For |x| in [0, 0.84375]\n69\t *        erf(x)  = x + x*R(x^2)\n70\t *          erfc(x) = 1 - erf(x)           if x in [-.84375,0.25]\n71\t *                  = 0.5 + ((0.5-x)-x*R)  if x in [0.25,0.84375]\n72\t *       where R = P/Q where P is an odd poly of degree 8 and\n73\t *       Q is an odd poly of degree 10.\n74\t *                         -57.90\n75\t *            | R - (erf(x)-x)/x | <= 2\n76\t *\n77\t *\n78\t *       Remark. The formula is derived by noting\n79\t *          erf(x) = (2/sqrt(pi))*(x - x^3/3 + x^5/10 - x^7/42 + ....)\n80\t *       and that\n81\t *          2/sqrt(pi) = 1.128379167095512573896158903121545171688\n82\t *       is close to one. The interval is chosen because the fix\n83\t *       point of erf(x) is near 0.6174 (i.e., erf(x)=x when x is\n84\t *       near 0.6174), and by some experiment, 0.84375 is chosen to\n85\t *        guarantee the error is less than one ulp for erf.\n86\t *\n87\t *      2. For |x| in [0.84375,1.25], let s = |x| - 1, and\n88\t *         c = 0.84506291151 rounded to single (24 bits)\n89\t *             erf(x)  = sign(x) * (c  + P1(s)/Q1(s))\n90\t *             erfc(x) = (1-c)  - P1(s)/Q1(s) if x > 0\n91\t *              1+(c+P1(s)/Q1(s))    if x < 0\n92\t *             |P1/Q1 - (erf(|x|)-c)| <= 2**-59.06\n93\t *       Remark: here we use the Tay