{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RsqBRXEa1ytBLMTbvRHSPE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/* SPDX-License-Identifier: SunMicrosystems */\n2\t/* Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved. */\n3\t\n4\t/**\n5\t *\n6\t * This family of functions multiplies the input value :math:`x` by an integral\n7\t * power of :math:`2`.\n8\t *\n9\t * Synopsis\n10\t * ========\n11\t *\n12\t * .. code-block:: c\n13\t *\n14\t *     #include <math.h>\n15\t *     float ldexpf(float x, int exp);\n16\t *     double ldexp(double x, int exp);\n17\t *     long double ldexpl(long double x, int exp);\n18\t *\n19\t * Description\n20\t * ===========\n21\t *\n22\t * ``ldexp`` multiplies the input value :math:`x` by an integral power of :math:`2`.\n23\t *\n24\t * ``ldexp`` and :ref:`scalbn` have the same functionality. In theory their\n25\t * definition could be different, but this only applies to architectures which\n26\t * do not use a binary system, which by now are assumed to be an obscurity.\n27\t *\n28\t * Mathematical Function\n29\t * =====================\n30\t *\n31\t * .. math::\n32\t *\n33\t *    ldexp(x, exp) \\approx x \\cdot 2^{exp}\n34\t *\n35\t * Returns\n36\t * =======\n37\t *\n38\t * ``ldexp`` returns the input value :math:`x` multiplied by :math:`2` powered\n39\t * by the input value :math:`exp`.\n40\t *\n41\t * Exceptions\n42\t * ==========\n43\t *\n44\t * Raise ``overflow`` exception if the result overflows.\n45\t *\n46\t * .. May raise ``underflow`` exception.\n47\t *\n48\t * Output map\n49\t * ==========\n50\t *\n51\t * +--------------+-------------------------+-----------+-------------------------+\n52\t * | ldexp(x,exp) | exp                                                           |\n53\t * +--------------+-------------------------+-----------+-------------------------+\n54\t * | x            | :math:`<0`              | :math:`0` | :math:`>0`              |\n55\t * +==============+=========================+===========+=========================+\n56\t * | :math:`-Inf` | :math:`x`               | :math:`x` | :math:`x`               |\n57\t * +--------------+-------------------------+           +-------------------------+\n58\t * | :math:`<0`   | :math:`x \\cdot 2^{exp}` |           | :math:`x \\cdot 2^{exp}` |\n59\t * +--------------+-------------------------+           +-------------------------+\n60\t * | :math:`-0`   | :math:`x`               |           | :math:`x`               |\n61\t * +--------------+                         +           +                         +\n62\t * | :math:`+0`   |                         |           |                         |\n63\t * +--------------+-------------------------+           +-------------------------+\n64\t * | :math:`>0`   | :math:`x \\cdot 2^{exp}` |           | :math:`x \\cdot 2^{exp}` |\n65\t * +--------------+-------------------------+           +-------------------------+\n66\t * | :math:`+Inf` | :math:`x`               |           | :math:`x`               |\n67\t * +--------------+-------------------------+-----------+-------------------------+\n68\t * | :math:`NaN`  | :math:`qNaN`                                                  |\n69\t * +--------------+-------------------------+-----------+-------------------------+\n70\t *\n71\t */\n72\t\n73\t#include <math.h>\n74\t\n75\t#ifndef __LIBMCS_DOUBLE_IS_32BITS\n76\t\n77\tdouble ldexp(double x, int exp)\n78\t{\n79\t#ifdef __LIBMCS_FPU_DAZ\n80\t    x *= __volatile_one;\n81\t#endif /* defined(__LIBMCS_FPU_DAZ) */\n82\t\n83\t    if ((isfinite(x) == 0) || (x == 0.0)) {\n84\t        return x + x;\n85\t    }\n86\t\n87\t    return scalbn(x, exp);\n88\t}\n89\t\n90\t#ifdef __LIBMCS_LONG_DOUBLE_IS_64BITS\n91\t\n92\tlong double ldexpl(long double x, int exp)\n93\t{\n94\t    return (long double) ldexp((double) x, exp);\n95\t}\n96\t\n97\t#endif /* #ifdef __LIBMCS_LONG_DOUBLE_IS_64BITS */\n98\t#endif /* #ifndef __LIBMCS_DOUBLE_IS_32BITS */\n99\t\n[result-id: r40]"}]},"parent_tool_use