========+\n    53\t * | **expm1(x)** | :math:`-1`    | :math:`e^x-1` | :math:`+0`              | :math:`e^x-1` | :math:`+Inf` | :math:`qNaN` |\n    54\t * +--------------+---------------+---------------+------------+------------+---------------+--------------+--------------+\n    55\t *\n    56\t */\n    57\t\n    58\t/* expm1(x)\n    59\t * Returns exp(x)-1, the exponential of x minus 1.\n    60\t *\n    61\t * Method\n    62\t *   1. Argument reduction:\n    63\t *    Given x, find r and integer k such that\n    64\t *\n    65\t *               x = k*ln2 + r,  |r| <= 0.5*ln2 ~ 0.34658\n    66\t *\n    67\t *      Here a correction term c will be computed to compensate\n    68\t *    the error in r when rounded to a floating-point number.\n    69\t *\n    70\t *   2. Approximating expm1(r) by a special rational function on\n    71\t *    the interval [0,0.34658]:\n    72\t *    Since\n    73\t *        r*(exp(r)+1)/(exp(r)-1) = 2+ r^2/6 - r^4/360 + ...\n    74\t *    we define R1(r*r) by\n    75\t *        r*(exp(r)+1)/(exp(r)-1) = 2+ r^2/6 * R1(r*r)\n    76\t *    That is,\n    77\t *        R1(r**2) = 6/r *((exp(r)+1)/(exp(r)-1) - 2/r)\n    78\t *             = 6/r * ( 1 + 2.0*(1/(exp(r)-1) - 1/r))\n    79\t *             = 1 - r^2/60 + r^4/2520 - r^6/100800 + ...\n    80\t *      We use a special Remez algorithm on [0,0.347] to generate\n    81\t *     a polynomial of degree 5 in r*r to approximate R1. The\n    82\t *    maximum error of this polynomial approximation is bounded\n    83\t *    by 2**-61. In other words,\n    84\t *        R1(z) ~ 1.0 + Q1*z + Q2*z**2 + Q3*z**3 + Q4*z**4 + Q5*z**5\n    85\t *    where     Q1  =  -1.6666666666666567384E-2,\n    86\t *              Q2  =   3.9682539681370365873E-4,\n    87\t *              Q3  =  -9.9206344733435987357E-6,\n    88\t *              Q4  =   2.5051361420808517002E-7,\n    89\t *              Q5  =  -6.2843505682382617102E-9;\n    90\t *      (where z=r*r, and the values of Q1 to Q5 are listed below)\n    91\t *    with error bounded by\n    92\t *        |                  5           |     -61\n    93\t *        | 1.0+Q1*z+...+Q5*z   -  R1(z) | <= 2\n    94\t *        |                              |\n    95\t *\n    96\t *    expm1(r) = exp(r)-1 is then computed by the following\n    97\t *     specific way which minimize the accumulation rounding error:\n    98\t *                   2     3\n    99\t *                  r     r    [ 3 - (R1 + R1*r/2)  ]\n   100\t *          expm1(r) = r + --- + --- * [--------------------]\n   101\t *                      2     2    [ 6 - r*(3 - R1*r/2) ]\n   102\t *\n   103\t *    To compensate the error in the argument reduction, we use\n   104\t *        expm1(r+c) = expm1(r) + c + expm1(r)*c\n   105\t *               ~ expm1(r) + c + r*c\n   106\t *    Thus c+r*c will be added in as the correction terms for\n   107\t *    expm1(r+c). Now rearrange the term to avoid optimization\n   108\t *     screw up:\n   109\t *                (      2                                    2 )\n   110\t *                ({  ( r    [ R1 -  (3 - R1*r/2) ]  )  }    r  )\n   111\t *     expm1(r+c)~r - ({r*(--- * [--------------------]-c)-c} - --- )\n   112\t *                    ({  ( 2    [ 6 - r*(3 - R1*r/2) ]  )  }    2  )\n   113\t *                      (                                             )\n   114\t *\n   115\t *           = r - E\n   116\t *   3. Scale back to obtain expm1(x):\n   117\t *    From step 1, we have\n   118\t *       expm1(x) = either 2^k*[expm1(r)+1] - 1\n   119\t *            = or     2^k*[expm1(r) + (1-2^-k)]\n   120\t *   4. Implementation notes:\n   121\t *    (A). To save one multiplication, we scale the coefficient Qi\n   122\t *         to Qi*2^i, and replace z by (x^2)/2.\n   123\t *    (B). To achieve maximum accuracy, we compute expm1(x) by\n   124\t *      (i)   if x < -56*ln2, return -1.0, (raise inexact if x!=inf)\n   125\t *      (ii)  if k=0, return r-E\n   126\t *      (iii) if k=-1, return 0.5*(r-