{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JhbMk5SYeqqvTUqaWTyq6S","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t/* SPDX-License-Identifier: SunMicrosystems */\n     2\t/* Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved. */\n     3\t\n     4\t/**\n     5\t *\n     6\t * This family of functions implements the natural logarithm of :math:`1 + x`.\n     7\t *\n     8\t * Synopsis\n     9\t * ========\n    10\t *\n    11\t * .. code-block:: c\n    12\t *\n    13\t *     #include <math.h>\n    14\t *     float log1pf(float x);\n    15\t *     double log1p(double x);\n    16\t *     long double logl(long double x);\n    17\t *\n    18\t * Description\n    19\t * ===========\n    20\t *\n    21\t * ``log1p`` computes the natural logarithm of :math:`1 + x`.\n    22\t *\n    23\t * Mathematical Function\n    24\t * =====================\n    25\t *\n    26\t * .. math::\n    27\t *\n    28\t *    log1p(x) \\approx ln(1 + x)\n    29\t *\n    30\t * Returns\n    31\t * =======\n    32\t *\n    33\t * ``log1p`` returns the natural logarithm of :math:`1 + x`.\n    34\t *\n    35\t * Exceptions\n    36\t * ==========\n    37\t *\n    38\t * Raise ``invalid operation`` exception when the input value is less than :math:`-1`.\n    39\t *\n    40\t * Raise ``divide by zero`` exception when the input value is :math:`-1`.\n    41\t *\n    42\t * .. May raise ``underflow`` exception.\n    43\t *\n    44\t * Output map\n    45\t * ==========\n    46\t *\n    47\t * +--------------+--------------+--------------+--------------+-------------------+------------+------------+-------------------+--------------+--------------+\n    48\t * | **x**        | :math:`-Inf` | :math:`<-1`  | :math:`-1`   | :math:`]-1,0[`    | :math:`-0` | :math:`+0` | :math:`>0`        | :math:`+Inf` | :math:`NaN`  |\n    49\t * +==============+==============+==============+==============+===================+============+============+===================+==============+==============+\n    50\t * | **log1p(x)** | :math:`qNaN` | :math:`qNaN` | :math:`-Inf` | :math:`ln(1 + x)` | :math:`x`               | :math:`ln(1 + x)` | :math:`+Inf` | :math:`qNaN` |\n    51\t * +--------------+--------------+--------------+--------------+-------------------+------------+------------+-------------------+--------------+--------------+\n    52\t *\n    53\t */\n    54\t\n    55\t/* double log1p(double x)\n    56\t *\n    57\t * Method :\n    58\t *   1. Argument Reduction: find k and f such that\n    59\t *            1+x = 2^k * (1+f),\n    60\t *       where  sqrt(2)/2 < 1+f < sqrt(2) .\n    61\t *\n    62\t *      Note. If k=0, then f=x is exact. However, if k!=0, then f\n    63\t *    may not be representable exactly. In that case, a correction\n    64\t *    term is need. Let u=1+x rounded. Let c = (1+x)-u, then\n    65\t *    log(1+x) - log(u) ~ c/u. Thus, we proceed to compute log(u),\n    66\t *    and add back the correction term c/u.\n    67\t *    (Note: when x > 2**53, one can simply return log(x))\n    68\t *\n    69\t *   2. Approximation of log1p(f).\n    70\t *    Let s = f/(2+f) ; based on log(1+f) = log(1+s) - log(1-s)\n    71\t *         = 2s + 2/3 s**3 + 2/5 s**5 + .....,\n    72\t *              = 2s + s*R\n    73\t *      We use a special Remez algorithm on [0,0.1716] to generate\n    74\t *     a polynomial of degree 14 to approximate R The maximum error\n    75\t *    of this polynomial approximation is bounded by 2**-58.45. In\n    76\t *    other words,\n    77\t *                2      4      6      8      10      12      14\n    78\t *        R(z) ~ Lp1*s +Lp2*s +Lp3*s +Lp4*s +Lp5*s  +Lp6*s  +Lp7*s\n    79\t *      (the values of Lp1 to Lp7 are listed in the program)\n    80\t *    and\n    81\t *        |      2          14          |     -58.45\n    82\t *        | Lp1*s +...+Lp7*s    -  R(z) | <= 2\n    83\t *        |                             |\n    84\t *    Note that 2s = f - s*f = f - hfsq + s*hfsq, where hfsq = f*f/2.\n    85\t *    In order to guarantee error in log below 1ulp, we compute log\n    86\t *    by\n    87\t *        log1p(f) = f - (hfsq - s*(hfsq+R)).\n    88\t *\n    89\t *    3. Finally, log1p(x) = k*ln2 + log1p(f).\n    90\t *                  = k*ln2_hi+(f-(hfsq-(s*(hfsq+R)+k*ln2_lo)))\n    91\t *       Here ln2 is split into two floating point number:\n    92\t *            ln2_hi + ln2_lo,\n    93\t *       where n*ln2_hi is always exact for |n| < 2000.\n    94\t *\n    95\t * Special cases:\n    96\t *    log1p(x) is NaN with signal if x < -1 (including -INF) ;\n    97\t *    log1p(+INF) is +INF; log1p(-1) is -INF with signal;\n    98\t *    log1p(NaN) is that NaN with no signal.\n    99\t *\n   100\t * Accuracy:\n   101\t *    according to an error analysis, the error is always less than\n   102\t *    1 ulp (unit in the last place).\n   103\t *\n   104\t * Constants:\n   105\t * The hexadecimal values are the intended ones for the following\n   106\t * constants. The decimal values may be used, provided that the\n   107\t * compiler will convert from decimal to binary accurately enough\n   108\t * to produce the hexadecimal values shown.\n   109\t *\n   110\t * Note: Assuming log() return accurate answer, the following\n   111\t *      algorithm can be used to compute log1p(x) to within a few ULP:\n   112\t *\n   113\t *        u = 1+x;\n   114\t *        if(u==1.0) return x ; else\n   115\t *               return log(u)*(x/(u-1.0));\n   116\t *\n   117\t *     See HP-15C Advanced Functions Handbook, p.193.\n   118\t */\n   119\t\n   120\t#include <math.h>\n   121\t#include \"../common/tools.h\"\n   122\t#include \"internal/log1pmfd.h\"\n   123\t\n   124\t#ifndef __LIBMCS_DOUBLE_IS_32BITS\n   125\t\n   126\tstatic const double\n   127\tln2_hi  =  6.93147180369123816490e-01,  /* 3fe62e42 fee00000 */\n   128\tln2_lo  =  1.90821492927058770002e-10;  /* 3dea39ef 35793c76 */\n   129\t\n   130\tstatic const double zero = 0.0;\n   131\t\n   132\tdouble log1p(double x)\n   133\t{\n   134\t#ifdef __LIBMCS_FPU_DAZ\n   135\t    x *= __volatile_one;\n   136\t#endif /* defined(__LIBMCS_FPU_DAZ) */\n   137\t\n   138\t    double hfsq, f, c, R, u;\n   139\t    int32_t k, hx, hu, ax;\n   140\t\n   141\t    c = NAN; /* initial value of c is never actually used */\n   142\t    f = NAN; /* initial value of f is never actually used */\n   143\t    hu = INT_MAX; /* initial value of hu is never actually used */\n   144\t\n   145\t    GET_HIGH_WORD(hx, x);\n   146\t    ax = hx & 0x7fffffff;\n   147\t\n   148\t    k = 1;\n   149\t\n   150\t    if (hx >= 0x7ff00000) {                /* x = NaN/+-Inf */\n   151\t        return x + x;\n   152\t    }\n   153\t\n   154\t    if (hx < 0x3FDA827A) {                 /* x < 0.41422  */\n   155\t        if (ax >= 0x3ff00000) {            /* x <= -1.0 */\n   156\t            if (isnan(x)) {\n   157\t                return x + x;\n   158\t            } else if (x == -1.0) {\n   159\t                return __raise_div_by_zero(-1.0); /* log1p(-1)=-inf */\n   160\t            } else {\n   161\t                return __raise_invalid(); /* log1p(x<-1)=NaN */\n   162\t            }\n   163\t        }\n   164\t\n   165\t        if (ax < 0x3e200000) {             /* |x| < 2**-29 */\n   166\t            if (ax < 0x3c900000) {         /* |x| < 2**-54 */\n   167\t                return __raise_inexact(x);\n   168\t            } else {\n   169\t                return __raise_inexact(x - x * x * 0.5);\n   170\t            }\n   171\t        }\n   172\t\n   173\t        if (hx > 0 || hx <= ((int32_t)0xbfd2bec3U)) {\n   174\t            k = 0;\n   175\t            f = x;\n   176\t            hu = 1;\n   177\t        }                                  /* -0.2929<x<0.41422 */\n   178\t    }\n   179\t\n   180\t    if (k != 0) {\n   181\t        if (hx < 0x43400000) {\n   182\t            u  = 1.0 + x;\n   183\t            GET_HIGH_WORD(hu, u);\n   184\t            k  = (hu >> 20) - 1023;\n   185\t            c  = (k > 0) ? 1.0 - (u - x) : x - (u - 1.0); /* correction term */\n   186\t            c /= u;\n   187\t        } else {\n   188\t            u  = x;\n   189\t            GET_HIGH_WORD(hu, u);\n   190\t            k  = (hu >> 20) - 1023;\n   191\t            c  = 0;\n   192\t        }\n   193\t\n   194\t        hu &= 0x000fffff;\n   195\t\n   196\t        if (hu < 0x6a09e) {\n   197\t            SET_HIGH_WORD(u, hu | 0x3ff00000); /* normalize u */\n   198\t        } else {\n   199\t            k += 1;\n   200\t            SET_HIGH_WORD(u, hu | 0x3fe00000); /* normalize u/2 */\n   201\t            hu = (0x00100000 - hu) >> 2;\n   202\t        }\n   203\t\n   204\t        f = u - 1.0;\n   205\t    }\n   206\t\n   207\t    hfsq = 0.5 * f * f;\n   208\t\n   209\t    if (hu == 0) { /* |f| < 2**-20 */\n   210\t        if (f == zero) {\n   211\t            c += k * ln2_lo;\n   212\t            return k * ln2_hi + c;\n   213\t        }\n   214\t\n   215\t        R = hfsq * (1.0 - 0.66666666666666666 * f);\n   216\t\n   217\t        return k * ln2_hi - ((R - (k * ln2_lo + c)) - f);\n   218\t    }\n   219\t\n   220\t    if (k == 0) {\n   221\t        return f - (hfsq - __log1pmf(f));\n   222\t    } else {\n   223\t        return k * ln2_hi - ((hfsq - (__log1pmf(f) + (k * ln2_lo + c))) - f);\n   224\t    }\n   225\t}\n   226\t\n   227\t#ifdef __LIBMCS_LONG_DOUBLE_IS_64BITS\n   228\t\n   229\tlong double log1pl(long double x)\n   230\t{\n   231\t    return (long double) log1p((double) x);\n   232\t}\n   233\t\n   234\t#endif /* #ifdef __LIBMCS_LONG_DOUBLE_IS_64BITS */\n   235\t#endif /* #ifndef __LIBMCS_DOUBLE_IS_32BITS */\n     1\t/* SPDX-License-Identifier: SunMicrosystems */\n     2\t/* Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved. */\n     3\t\n     4\t/**\n     5\t *\n     6\t * This family of functions computes the binary exponent of the input value.\n     7\t *\n     8\t * Synopsis\n     9\t * ========\n    10\t *\n    11\t * .. code-block:: c\n    12\t *\n    13\t *     #include <math.h>\n    14\t *     float logbf(float x);\n    15\t *     double logb(double x);\n    16\t *     long double logbl(long double x);\n    17\t *\n    18\t * Description\n    19\t * ===========\n    20\t *\n    21\t * ``logb`` computes the binary exponent of the input value.\n    22\t *\n    23\t * ``logb`` and :ref:`ilogb` have the same functionality, but ``logb`` returns\n    24\t * the binary exponent as a floating-point value while :ref:`ilogb` returns a\n    25\t * signed integer.\n    26\t *\n    27\t * Mathematical Function\n    28\t * =====================\n    29\t *\n    30\t * .. math::\n    31\t *\n    32\t *    logb(x) \\approx \\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor\n    33\t *\n    34\t * Returns\n    35\t * =======\n    36\t *\n    37\t * ``logb`` returns the binary exponent of the input value.\n    38\t *\n    39\t * Exceptions\n    40\t * ==========\n    41\t *\n    42\t * Raise ``divide by zero`` exception when the input value is zero.\n    43\t *\n    44\t * Output map\n    45\t * ==========\n    46\t *\n    47\t * +-------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+--------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+--------------+--------------+\n    48\t * | **x**       | :math:`-Inf` | :math:`<0`                           | :math:`-0`   | :math:`+0`   | :math:`>0`                           | :math:`+Inf` | :math:`NaN`  |\n    49\t * +=============+==============+======================================+==============+==============+======================================+==============+==============+\n    50\t * | **logb(x)** | :math:`+Inf` | :math:`\\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor` | :math:`-Inf`                | :math:`\\lfloor {\\log_2 |x|} \\rfloor` | :math:`+Inf` | :math:`qNaN` |\n    51\t * +-------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+--------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+--------------+--------------+\n    52\t *\n    53\t */\n    54\t\n    55\t#include <math.h>\n    56\t#include \"../common/tools.h\"\n    57\t\n    58\t#ifndef __LIBMCS_DOUBLE_IS_32BITS\n    59\t\n    60\tdouble logb(double x)\n    61\t{\n    62\t#ifdef __LIBMCS_FPU_DAZ\n    63\t    x *= __volatile_one;\n    64\t#endif /* defined(__LIBMCS_FPU_DAZ) */\n    65\t\n    66\t    int32_t hx, lx, ix;\n    67\t\n    68\t    EXTRACT_WORDS(hx, lx, x);\n    69\t    hx &= 0x7fffffff;        /* high |x| */\n    70\t\n    71\t    if (hx < 0x00100000) {     /* 0 or subnormal */\n    72\t        if ((hx | lx) == 0)  {\n    73\t            return __raise_div_by_zero(-1.0);  /* logb(0) = -inf */\n    74\t        } else {         /* subnormal x */\n    75\t            if (hx == 0) {\n    76\t                for (ix = -1043; lx > 0; lx <<= 1) {\n    77\t                    ix -= 1;\n    78\t                }\n    79\t            } else {\n    80\t                for (ix = -1022, hx <<= 11; hx > 0; hx <<= 1) {\n    81\t                    ix -= 1;\n    82\t                }\n    83\t            }\n    84\t        }\n    85\t\n    86\t        return (double) ix;\n    87\t    } else if (hx < 0x7ff00000) {\n    88\t        return (hx >> 20) - 1023;    /* normal # */\n    89\t    } else {\n    90\t        return x * x;    /* x = NaN/+-Inf */\n    91\t    }\n    92\t}\n    93\t\n    94\t#ifdef __LIBMCS_LONG_DOUBLE_IS_64BITS\n    95\t\n    96\tlong double logbl(long double x)\n    97\t{\n    98\t    return (long double) logb((double) x);\n    99\t}\n   100\t\n   101\t#endif /* #ifdef __LIBMCS_LONG_DOUBLE_IS_64BITS */\n   102\t#endif /* #ifndef __LIBMCS_DOUBLE_IS_32BITS */\n[result-id: r13]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HHn2CoSr5VKbaWMe7ZDA6P","session_id":"d923b022-feac-4b63-bc89-51a1cb4c0215","uuid":"89eee781-f745-4c46-82b1-6dcb17510c42","timestamp":"2026-04-07T18:51:10.357Z"}
